Bug 2077903 - Abort feed downloads that stop receiving data. r=thunderbird-back-end-reviewers,edicharry

Once a feed response started loading, the request timeout was cleared so
large feeds could complete. A server that sent a partial response and then
stalled kept the request pending forever, holding the feed in FeedCache and
blocking further subscriptions.

Replace the cleared timeout with an inactivity timer that is reset on each
progress event and aborts the request if no data arrives within
FeedUtils.REQUEST_TIMEOUT.

Differential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D331127

